prompt.text:
Implement a new TypeScript API for managing an immutable queue of transient banners.

Export these declarations:

```ts
export type BannerKind = "positive" | "neutral" | "caution" | "negative";
export interface Banner { readonly id: string; readonly kind: BannerKind; readonly text: string; readonly ttlMs: number; }
export function enqueueBanner(queue: readonly Banner[], input: { id: string; kind: BannerKind; text: string; ttlMs?: number }): Banner[];
export function dismissBanner(queue: readonly Banner[], id: string): Banner[];
```

`enqueueBanner` must trim `id` and `text`, reject an empty trimmed value for either by throwing `TypeError`, and use 4000 when `ttlMs` is omitted. A supplied lifetime must be a finite integer from 0 through 60,000 inclusive; otherwise throw `RangeError`. If the normalized ID already exists, replace that entry in its current position. Otherwise append the banner. `dismissBanner` must remove every entry whose ID exactly equals the supplied ID while preserving order. Both functions must return new arrays and must never mutate the input array or its banner objects. No input aliases may be stored in the result. Return a complete source file using only the standard language/runtime APIs.

